{title: 150 - Who Is He in Yonder Stall?}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #150 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 150}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Gm]Who is He [Eb]in [Ab]yonder [Gm]stall,
[Gm]At whose feet the shepherds fall?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Fm/C]'Tis the Lord, O [Bb]wondrous story,
[Cm]'Tis [Fm]the Lord, the King [Ab]of glory!
[Bb]At His [Eb]feet we [Gm]humbly [Bb]fall,
[C7]Crown Him, [Cm]crown Him Lord of [Eb/Bb]all.
[Eb]At His feet [Bb]we [Bb7]humbly [Bb]fall- [Gm]the Lord [Bb]of all.
[Bb]Crown [Cm]Him, [Bb]crown Him, Jesus, [Fm]Jesus,
[Cm/G]Crown Him Lord of all.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Gm]Who is He [Eb]in [Ab]deep [Gm]distress,
[Gm]Fasting in the wilderness?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Gm]Who is He, the [Ab]gathering [Gm]throng
[Gm]Greet with loud triumphant song?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Gm]Lo, at midnight, [Ab]who [Gm]is He
[Gm]Prays in dark Gethsemane?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[Gm]Who is He [Eb]on [Ab]yonder [Gm]tree
[Gm]Dies in shame and agony?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
[Gm]Who is He [Eb]that [Ab]from [Gm]the grave
[Gm]Comes to heal and help and save?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 7}
[Gm]Who is He [Eb]that [Ab]from [Gm]His throne
[Gm]Rules through all the world alone?
{end_of_verse}
